{"id":"torrey:publicans","source":"torrey","name":"Publicans","slug":"publicans","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"The collectors of the public taxes — Lu 5:27.","refs":[["Luke",5,27,5,27]]},{"text":"Suspected of extortion — Lu 3:13.","refs":[["Luke",3,13,3,13]]},{"text":"Often guilty of extortion — Lu 19:8.","refs":[["Luke",19,8,19,8]]},{"text":"Chiefs of, were very rich — Lu 19:2.","refs":[["Luke",19,2,19,2]]},{"text":"Despised. — Lu 18:11.","refs":[["Luke",18,11,18,11]]},{"text":"Classed with the most infamous characters. — Mt 11:19; 21:32.","refs":[["Matt",11,19,11,19],["Matt",21,32,21,32]]},{"text":"Despised our Lord for associating with. — Mt 9:11; 11:19.","refs":[["Matt",9,11,9,11],["Matt",11,19,11,19]]},{"text":"Often kind to their friends — Mt 5:46,47.","refs":[["Matt",5,46,5,46],["Matt",5,47,5,47]]},{"text":"Often hospitable — Lu 5:29; 19:6.","refs":[["Luke",5,29,5,29],["Luke",19,6,19,6]]},{"text":"Believed the preaching of John. — Mt 21:32.","refs":[["Matt",21,32,21,32]]},{"text":"Received John’s baptism. — Lu 3:12; 7:29.","refs":[["Luke",3,12,3,12],["Luke",7,29,7,29]]},{"text":"Attended the preaching of Christ. — Mr 2:15; Lu 15:1.","refs":[["Mark",2,15,2,15],["Luke",15,1,15,1]]},{"text":"Embraced the gospel. — Mt 21:31.","refs":[["Matt",21,31,21,31]]},{"text":"Matthew the apostle was of — Mt 10:3.","refs":[["Matt",10,3,10,3]]}],"refCount":20}
